course: dictionary
lesson: 5516
title: Leak: a drip, a hole or a secret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leak is when something gets out through a hole or crack, usually by accident. Water can leak from a pipe, and gas can leak from a cooker. As a verb, «to leak» means to let something escape. As a noun, «a leak» is the small hole or crack itself.
explain: «When one site leaks passwords, criminals try the same email and password on other sites.» Here leaks passwords means lets passwords get out to people who should not have them. It works like a secret being told, so you can tell the word is about escaping, even though nothing is dripping.
explain: «Hawking's leaking» in the example sentence is harder, so use the clues. A leak is a thing escaping from somewhere it should stay. If you read «a lot of what you hear at home is that work leaking in», you can work out that leaking in means getting through into a place where it does not belong.
explain: «Natural gas has no smell, so companies add a smelly chemical to make leaks noticeable.» The sentence tells you that a gas leak is something you must notice. Real gas leaks smell like rotten eggs, and if you smell one, leave the house and tell an adult.
fact: A leak is a small hole or crack that lets things through, or the liquid or gas that escapes.
fact: «To leak» means to let liquid or gas escape through a hole or crack by accident.
fact: «To leak a secret» means to tell it to people who should not know.
fact: A gas leak is an emergency: leave the house, tell an adult, and do not switch lights on or off.
fact: Batteries can leak harmful liquid, so do not touch it.
exercise: «The bath tap had a slow leak, and water dripped onto the floor all night.» What is a leak? | A kind of soap | *A small hole or crack that lets liquid through | A bathroom tile | A loud noise from a pipe
exercise: «The roof began to leak when it rained.» Find and copy one word that means to let water escape through a crack. | began | rained | *leak | roof
exercise: «When Priya leaked the secret, her friends were upset.» What does leaked the secret mean? | Forgot the secret completely | *Told the secret to people who should not know | Wrote the secret on the wall | Kept the secret safe in a box
test: «A gas leak has a smell like rotten eggs.» What should you do if you smell a gas leak? | Switch the lights on to see better | Stay inside and open the windows | *Leave the house and tell an adult | Ignore it, it is probably nothing
test: «Batteries can leak harmful liquid.» What should you do with a leaking battery? | Shake it hard to stop it | Put it in your mouth to test it | Lick it to see what it is | *Do not touch it, and tell an adult
exam: «When one site leaks passwords, criminals try the same email and password on other sites.» What stops one leak opening everything? | Writing passwords on sticky notes on your screen | Using the same password everywhere | Sharing your password with friends | *Using different passwords for different sites
